  "faq_heading": "Surrey schools: your questions answered",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The BC Ministry of Education and Child Care school list shows 168 schools with a Surrey street address: 137 public schools and 31 independent schools. It also shows 9 college and university campuses."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Public schools here are run by School District 36 (Surrey) and School District 93 (Conseil scolaire francophone). Count by district: School District 36 (Surrey): 136, School District 93 (Conseil scolaire francophone): 1."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The list includes alternate programs, continuing education centres and online schools that have a street address, so the totals run higher than the number of neighbourhood schools. The Ministry's own level field also mislabels some secondary schools as elementary, so this page reads the level from the school's name."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "If you are buying with a child in mind, the address matters more than the list. A school's catchment decides which children it must take, and districts change catchments and set their own rules for French immersion and other programs. Ask the district about the exact address before you write an offer."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The list covers the whole city, so schools in South Surrey, Cloverdale, Newton, Fleetwood and Guildford are in it because they carry Surrey addresses."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Read how South Surrey school catchments work",
      "h": "/south-surrey-school-catchments.html"
    },
